cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "transport-xr-grid: the meshing pen's input surface"
abstract: >
  A Godot 4.4 XR project holding the hand end of the meshing pen: a stroke
  sketcher that builds an ArrayMesh, pinch and world-grab interaction, a GPU
  trail that draws the stroke as it is made, a procedural infinite grid to
  place it against, and the OpenXR action map that binds a controller to all
  of it. On the hexagon it is a transport layer, because it terminates the
  protocol a pair of hands speaks and triggers the interactor that turns a
  closed stroke into geometry.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
  - alias: celyk
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-xr-grid"
keywords:
  - godot
  - openxr
  - sketching
  - user-generated-content

references:

  # ── What this is a fork of ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - type: software
    title: "V-Sekai.xr-grid"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
      - alias: celyk
    year: 2026
    license: MIT
    url: "https://github.com/V-Sekai/transport-xr-grid"
    notes: >
      Forked rather than read. This project may write to its own organisation and
      not to V-Sekai's, and a mission whose whole content is that anyone can build
      in world cannot keep the surface they build with somewhere it may only read.
      The README stays upstream's; `Lib.mirrors/0` in infrastructure-logbook records
      the parent.

  # ── The engine it is a project for ───────────────────────────────────────────
  - type: software
    title: "Godot Engine"
    authors:
      - name: "Juan Linietsky, Ariel Manzur and the Godot contributors"
    year: 2026
    version: "4.4"
    license: MIT
    url: "https://godotengine.org"
    notes: >
      `project.godot` asks for 4.4 with Double Precision and Forward Plus. Double
      precision is not incidental: a world players keep building into is one whose
      coordinates get large, and single-precision jitter is what stops that being
      true far from the origin.

  # ── Standards the input surface speaks ───────────────────────────────────────
  - type: software
    title: "OpenXR"
    authors:
      - name: "The Khronos Group Inc."
    year: 2026
    license: Apache-2.0
    url: "https://www.khronos.org/openxr/"
    notes: >
      `openxr_action_map.tres` binds the pinch, grab and draw actions. OpenXR is a
      trademark of The Khronos Group Inc., and this project is not affiliated with
      or endorsed by them.
